{
  "subtree_index": [
    {
      "path": "design-system",
      "summary": "Browser-based design prototype with shared styles, fixture data, two inventory layouts, a new-frame wizard and master data screens.",
      "interface": [
        "The HTML entry point loads React, ReactDOM and Babel from a CDN, then local CSS and JSX. App mounts at #root. [Frame Inventory.html:script] [app.jsx:App]",
        "The shared browser interfaces expose fixture frames, status metadata, filter options, pin positions and reusable UI components. [data.jsx:window.FRAME_DATA] [shell.jsx:Object.assign]",
        "Direction A offers a filter sidebar, table or map and separate frame screens. Direction B keeps a searchable list beside map, detail, edit and history panes. [direction-a.jsx:DirA] [direction-a.jsx:DirA_Search] [direction-b.jsx:DirB]",
        "The five-step frame wizard and four master data screens are reachable from app navigation. [master-data.jsx:NewFrameScreen] [master-data.jsx:MD_CONTENT] [shell.jsx:Rail]"
      ],
      "invariants": [
        "The app defaults to Direction A, comfortable density and search. Direction changes return to frame search. [app.jsx:DEFAULT_TWEAKS] [app.jsx:App]",
        "Both directions default to frame FRM-00214 and fall back to the first fixture if a selection fails to resolve. [direction-a.jsx:DirA] [direction-b.jsx:DirB]",
        "The wizard initializes draft status and takes the first region, site type and technology from the fixture data. [master-data.jsx:NewFrameScreen]"
      ],
      "side_effects": [
        "Script initialization fills empty fixture histories and exposes data and components on window. [data.jsx:FRAMES.forEach] [data.jsx:window.FRAME_DATA] [shell.jsx:Object.assign]",
        "Frame saves and cancellations return to detail. Creating a frame returns to the frame section, and master data saves close the drawer. Fixture records remain unchanged. [direction-a.jsx:DirA_Edit] [direction-b.jsx:DirB_Edit] [direction-b.jsx:DirB] [master-data.jsx:NewFrameScreen] [master-data.jsx:MDDrawer] [app.jsx:App]",
        "Tweak updates send edits to the parent and dispatch a local event. The panel listens for host activation and can read rail visibility from local storage and send rail toggles to the current window. [tweaks-panel.jsx:useTweaks] [tweaks-panel.jsx:TweaksPanel]"
      ]
    }
  ]
}

